  "worked_solution": "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14100085/assets/5d56dfdb75870a251f1eb94f0305a083489ce9e8dc4b9843138cd8ef88da30ab.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,2{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 4x+6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y}}{y+1}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{4x+6}\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y}}{y+1}\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$",
